      nursingEssentials: ["Confirm dose, frequency, indication, last injection, LDL response, storage, warming time, device integrity, site rotation, complete injection, and sharps disposal.", "For monthly dosing, follow the current device instructions and missed-dose algorithm exactly; do not compress or double doses by intuition."],
      interactions: ["No meaningful CYP-mediated interactions are expected because antibodies are cleared by proteolysis rather than cytochrome enzymes. Continue indicated background lipid therapy unless the prescriber changes it.", "Other injectable therapies, allergy history, and immunologic disease still matter because they change reaction recognition and adherence planning."],
      keyLabs: ["Lipid panel at a time that reflects the chosen dosing interval; no routine alirocumab level is used.", "Unexpected response should prompt administration, storage, access, adherence, diagnosis, and receptor-function review before automatic dose escalation."],
      nclexTraps: ["Alirocumab and evolocumab share a mechanism but have different labels, devices, strengths, schedules, and age indications.", "Alirocumab is an antibody against PCSK9 protein, not an RNA drug and not a statin."],
      populationRisks: populationRisks("Current labeling includes selected pediatric familial hypercholesterolemia use; apply the current age and dose criteria.", "Older adults usually need no age-only adjustment, but dexterity, cognition, and injection support determine feasibility.", "Human pregnancy and lactation data are limited; specialist risk-benefit review is appropriate for severe inherited or established disease."),
      sourceNote: "Current U.S. Praluent label: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7bcfbac2-e8ac-4569-8edc-bcde3b1fd172",
